# FIN PHY — hidden-memory continuation

Date: 2026-09-23

## Scope

This campaign continues the operational-carrier package.  The finite `C12`
carrier is treated as already recovered at the one-jump level.  The new question
is whether that one-jump law forces a Markov path law, and if not, what finite
multi-step records can falsify hidden memory.

No physical system or external event record is used.

## OCB-MEM-01A — exact horizon aliases

Let `p` be the 11-outcome strict embedded-jump increment distribution and define

`c=+1` on distance-one increments,
`c=-1` on distance-two increments,
and `c=0` otherwise.

For `0<delta<0.11566747562103387`, both `p+delta c` and `p-delta c` are
probability laws.

Choose `L` hidden fair signs `Z_0,...,Z_(L-1)` and at visible jump `t` use

`p + delta Z_(t mod L) c`.

The ordered hidden sign word rotates deterministically, so this is a finite
hidden-state model.

### Exact theorem

For every `n<=L`, averaging the hidden signs factor by factor gives exactly

`P_alias(R_0,...,R_(n-1)) = product_t p(R_t)`.

At `n=L+1`, the first and last increments reuse the same hidden sign and

`P_alias - P_strict = delta^2 c tensor p^(tensor(L-1)) tensor c`.

Therefore

`TV(P_alias,P_strict) = 8 delta^2`,

independent of `L`.

At the frozen audit value `delta=0.05`, the exact first discrepancy is `TV=0.02`.
For `L=2`, the complete two-step law agrees with strict to numerical replay
error `2.9e-17`, while the complete three-step law has `TV=0.02`.
The endpoint contrast witness has expectation gap

`16 delta^2 = 0.04`.

### Consequence

There is no model-independent finite path horizon that excludes *all* finite
hidden-memory aliases.  For any predeclared horizon, a larger finite hidden
model can postpone its first discrepancy beyond that horizon.

This is an identifiability theorem, not a physical hidden-environment claim.

## OCB-MEM-01B — persistent two-state memory

Let `h_t in {+1,-1}` be a stationary two-state Markov chain with

`E[h_t h_(t+l)] = rho^l`.

Conditioned on `h_t`, the visible increment law is

`p + delta h_t c`.

The visible one-step law is exactly `p` for every `delta,rho`.

The exact two-step law is

`p(a)p(b) + delta^2 rho c(a)c(b)`,

so

`TV_2 = 8 delta^2 |rho|`.

For the contrast random variable `C_t=c(R_t)`,

`Cov(C_t,C_(t+l)) = 16 delta^2 rho^l`.

Hence, when memory is nonzero,

`rho = C_2/C_1`,

`delta^2 = C_1^2/(16 C_2)`.

Thus two-step data detect this declared memory class and three-step data
separate persistence from contrast amplitude.

For the synthetic stress point `delta=0.05,rho=0.8`, the two-step TV is
`0.016`, lag-one covariance is `0.032`, lag-two covariance is `0.0256`, and an
ideal equal-prior Chernoff upper bound reaches 5 percent error after 7,940
independent two-jump records.  This number is a synthetic power diagnostic,
not a laboratory recommendation.

## OCB-MEM-01C — bounded hidden dimension

A finite hidden-state output process with `H` hidden states has a weighted-matrix
word representation of dimension at most `H`.  The strict iid embedded-jump law
has dimension one.  Their difference therefore has dimension at most `H+1`.

For a `d`-dimensional linear representation

`s(w)=alpha M_w beta`,

the reachable row spaces generated by words of length at most `n` can strictly
increase at most `d-1` times.  If `s(w)=0` for all words of length at most
`d-1`, a basis of the full reachable space is orthogonal to `beta`, so `s(w)=0`
for every word.

Therefore:

> If an `H`-state hidden model and the strict iid path law agree on every visible
> word of lengths `0,...,H`, they agree at every length.  Any inequivalent
> `H`-state hidden model has a witness of length at most `H`.

This is the standard finite-equivalence principle for probabilistic/weighted
automata specialized here to FIN jump records.  The FIN-specific contribution
is the explicit clock-free alias family and frozen witnesses above.

Controls:

- the two-hidden-state persistent model has its first witness at length `2`,
  saturating its bound;
- the four-state period-two alias has a witness at length `3`, below its general
  bound `4`.

A bound on `H` is itself an additional model/operational premise until it is
measured or otherwise justified.

## Decision

`OCB-MEM-01 = PASS_WITH_IDENTIFIABILITY_BOUNDARY`.

One-jump carrier recovery does not imply Markov dynamics.  Multi-step path
records can falsify declared bounded-memory classes, but unrestricted finite
memory has no universal predeclared testing horizon.
